.TH BACKGROUND 2 2000-1月 "geneSet.annotations" "geneSet.annotations"
.SH NAME
geneSet.annotations \- Make the gene set annotation via a given GSEA background model.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIgeneSet.annotations(\fBbackground\fR as <generic> Background, 
\fBgeneSet\fR as any, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Make the gene set annotation via a given GSEA background model.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBbackground\fB \fR\- the GSEA background model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgeneSet\fB \fR\- 
 the gene id set that will be annotated, could be a character vector of the gene ids
 or a \fBdataframe\fR object whose row names are the gene ids. When a \fBdataframe\fR is
 given the annotation columns will be appended to it directly.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a \fBdataframe\fR with the gene id as the row names and the columns of the cluster
 information (\fBcluster\fR, \fBclusterName\fR, \fBcategory\fR, \fBclass\fR and the
 annotation terms) of each gene.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
background
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
